Val-Dwa-Law

A bold girl by the name of Tower had decended the Dungeons of Doom and
not died straight away....strange I thought....my knowledge of the game
was coming on in leaps and bounds!

To start at the beginning I bashed monsters until I was Level 5 then
gained Excalibur, this made things much simpler....ran around the
dungeon for a while hitting things, found a bag of holding early on
which I blessed. converted a couple of alters and killed a priest....
stuffed the bag full of potions, all identified thanks to unicorn horn
and lots of quaffing... also full of scrolls and spellbooks.
cleared out down to the Medusa level (no Big Room) went back and did
the Mines.

At this point I still hadn't identified "identify" (no general shops!)
or found a lamp.....did have loads of candles though - thanks Izchak!

on the way back down to the Medusa level - I went to the quest - one
level too early, came back....

very tough by this point with 150HP, $14000, AC only -3 but with
AoR.....

Got down to Medusa level - first time i'd been there.....gremlims
everywhere, fell in the water - goodbye potions and scrolls. crossed
the water by potion...
got to medusa, smashed her statue ;)
descended into maze.....got level teleported back to level 9
.=2E..!!!?$!!"=A3"!!!=AC=AC!=AC!

On he way back down tooled myself up with scrolls of earth, levitation,
more potions to replace those diluted and more scrolls.

made a lot of holy water.

crossed to the island again, got through the maze. got to the next
level to find another level new to me....pushed boulders into the water
and walked across.

hindsight is a wonderful thing. couldn't work out why I couldn't run
through a gap to escape two Xorns.....the gap was a drawbridge
obviously....

Tower, Val-Dwa-Law 270,000 points killed by 2 Xorns whilst banging head
into a drawbridge....

